1. Active Listening: Listen to your spouse's perspective and try to understand their point of view. This can help you identify areas of agreement and disagreement, and create a shared understanding of the conflict.
2. Active Listening: Pay attention to your spouse's words and actions. This can help you identify patterns or triggers that may be contributing to the conflict.
