[The Start of Assistant 1’s Answer]
The stages of life are a universal experience, and they shape our understanding of time and mortality in a number of ways.  First, they give us a sense of order and progression to our lives, as we move from infancy to childhood to adulthood and eventually to old age.  This progression gives us a sense of direction and purpose, and also helps us to understand that time is passing and we are moving closer to death.  The different stages of life also provide a framework for making sense of our experiences and emotions, as we encounter new challenges, responsibilities, and feelings at each stage of life.  Finally, the stages of life can help us to appreciate the present moment, as we are reminded that our time is limited and we should make the most of each day.
